  "assumptions": [
    "Idealized model: small swings, period T = 2π√(L/g) with g = 9.81 m/s²; exact in the model, approximately true of a real pendulum.",
    "The string is light and doesn't stretch, and the bob is treated as a point at the string's end.",
    "No air resistance or friction, so the swing never dies down. The starting angle is fixed at 10°.",
    "Changing the length recomputes the swing from the current time, so the bob may jump to a new point in its swing. The loop restarts every 30 s.",
    "Large-angle swings, where the real period grows slightly, and damping are not shown."
  ],
  "program": {
    "source": "export function evaluate({ inputs, time }) {\n  const L = inputs.length;\n  const T = 2 * Math.PI * Math.sqrt(L / 9.81);\n  const th = 0.1745 * Math.cos(2 * Math.PI * time / T);\n  return {\n    nodes: {\n      arm: { quaternion: [0, 0, Math.sin(th / 2), Math.cos(th / 2)] },\n      str: { position: [0, -L / 2, 0], scale: [1, L, 1] },\n      bobN: { position: [0, -L, 0] }\n    },\n    readouts: { period: T, len: L }\n  };\n}"
  }
